1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,800
Consider a shopper deciding
whether to buy another shirt.

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:12,000
THREADROOM compares that possibility with
an owned alternative, in one fitting workspace.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,500
These sample garments represent the two choices.
Both use the same fictional adult input.

4
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:23,500
The navy shirt stands in for an item
already in the wardrobe.

5
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:28,000
No try-on has been generated yet.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,000
With permission to use these images,
I confirm consent and start the try-on.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:43,000
The selected photos go through the private PHP server
to YouCam's cloth-v3 clothing virtual try-on API.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,000
YouCam processes the garments asynchronously.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,500
THREADROOM checks each existing task,
rather than creating another when a response is slow.

10
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:57,000
This edit shortens the processing wait.

11
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:02,000
What follows must be the actual results
from these inputs.

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Here are the two genuine YouCam outputs.

13
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,000
I can compare A and B,
then check either against the original.

14
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:17,500
The labels keep input and AI output distinct.

15
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:23,000
This is a visual impression, not a guarantee
of size, comfort or physical fit.

16
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Now I add an illustrative price of sixty
and thirty expected wears.

17
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Two per wear is simple division,
based on these inputs.

18
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,000
A note keeps the decision personal.

19
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,000
The app does not predict habits
or tell anyone what to buy.

20
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:46,000
The workspace includes English,
Traditional Chinese and Japanese.

21
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:51,500
Saving notes or a comparison image
is an explicit local download.

22
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:56,000
It does not publish a photo
or create a public gallery.

23
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Clear removes this page's data
and requests server cleanup.

24
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Pending cleanup stays visible.
Provider retention still applies,

25
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,000
and downloaded files remain on the device.

26
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,500
THREADROOM. Compare something new
with something you already love.

27
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:15,000
The working demo and source
are in the description.
